reference/plugins/mastra.content:
## Enabled

This plugin is enabled if `"mastra"` is listed in `"dependencies"` or `"devDependencies"` in `package.json`.

## Default configuration

If this plugin is enabled, the following configuration is added automatically:

```json
{
  "mastra": {
    "entry": [
      "src/mastra/index.{js,ts}",
      "src/mastra/{storage,observability,logger,server,studio}.{js,ts,mjs,mts}",
      "src/mastra/workflows/*.{js,ts}",
      "src/mastra/{,agents/*/}tools/**/*.{js,ts}",
      "src/mastra/agents/*/*(subagents/*/){config,instructions,memory,workspace}.{js,ts}",
      "src/mastra/agents/*/*(subagents/*/){tools,scorers,skills,processors/input,processors/output}/*.{js,ts}",
      "src/mastra/agents/*/*(subagents/*/)schedules/**/*.{js,ts}",
      "!src/mastra/**/*.{test,spec}.{js,ts}",
      "!src/mastra/**/__tests__/**"
    ]
  }
}
```

Depending on local configuration, plugins may modify the defaults as shown.

Custom `config` or `entry` options override default values, they are not merged.

See [Plugins](explanations/plugins) for more details about plugins and their `entry` and `config` options.

## Shell commands

This plugin adds argument parsing for the <code>mastra</code>
binary. Configuration:

```
string: ["dir", "tools"]
alias: {"dir": ["d"], "tools": ["t"]}
resolveInputs: (parsed, { cwd }) => {
    if (!discoveryCommands.has(parsed._[0])) return [];
    const inputs = [];
    if (parsed.dir) {
      for (const pattern of getProductionPatterns(parsed.dir)) inputs.push(toProductionEntry(pattern));
    }
    if (parsed.tools) {
      // `--tools` takes a comma-separated list of tool files, globs or directories; Mastra bundles each match
      // as its own input and imports them all from the generated `tools.mjs`, so each is an entry file.
      for (const tool of String(parsed.tools).split(',')) {
        const specifier = tool.trim();
        if (!specifier) continue;
        const pattern = isDirectory(join(cwd, specifier)) ? `${specifier}/index.${extensions}` : specifier;
        inputs.push(toProductionEntry(pattern));
      }
    }
    return inputs;
  }
```

The configuration was generated from source code. Also see [Script Parser](features/script-parser).

